<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20696] Get rid of already expired time guards in Lustre</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20696</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Alreadyexpiredguardsnobodynoticed"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Already-expired guards nobody noticed&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The current version is 2.17.58, so every &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt; 2.16.53&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt; 2.17.53&lt;/tt&gt; guard has &lt;b&gt;already&lt;/b&gt; fired, silently:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_lproc.c:39&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;lustre/osd-zfs/osd_lproc.c:26&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt; 2.17.53&lt;/tt&gt;) removed the &lt;tt&gt;symlink_brw_stats&lt;/tt&gt; module parameter. A site with &lt;tt&gt;options osd_ldiskfs symlink_brw_stats=1&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;modprobe.d&lt;/tt&gt; now gets, on a current build: &lt;tt&gt;osd_ldiskfs: unknown parameter 'symlink_brw_stats' ignored&lt;/tt&gt;. The module still loads; the setting is silently dropped and &lt;tt&gt;brw_stats&lt;/tt&gt; never appears where the admin expected it. Nothing failed loudly.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lustre/ptlrpc/sec_lproc.c:173,259&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;lustre/utils/l_getsepol.c:498&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt; 2.16.53&lt;/tt&gt;) dropped the old SELinux-policy downcall magic on both sides at once. Fine as long as &lt;tt&gt;l_getsepol&lt;/tt&gt; and the kernel modules are upgraded together; it silently breaks a mixed userspace/kernel install.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lustre/utils/obd.c:4743&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;&amp;gt; 2.17.52&lt;/tt&gt;) and &lt;tt&gt;:5427&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;&amp;gt; 2.17.53&lt;/tt&gt;) started printing deprecation notices to &lt;b&gt;stdout&lt;/b&gt;, which any test parsing &lt;tt&gt;lctl nodemap_*&lt;/tt&gt; output will see.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
